  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in maritime security incidents give US policymakers political cover and intelligence evidence to broaden export controls, sanctions and compliance requirements targeting Chinese access to AI compute and cloud services.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_us_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_maritime_war::maritime_security_risk" target="china_us_tech_trade::ai_compute_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened maritime attacks and convoy risks disrupt shipments of GPUs, servers and spare parts and force cloud providers to throttle or relocate workloads, reducing available AI compute capacity that depends on cross-border hardware flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_us_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_maritime_war::maritime_security_risk" target="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher maritime security risk increases the likelihood of attacks and insurance/operational losses, prompting primary dealers and market-makers to pull back, widen bid-ask spreads and reduce inventory, thereby lowering bond market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_maritime_war::maritime_security_risk" target="global_bond_turmoil::nominal_treasury_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating maritime security risk produces a flight-to-quality as investors seek safe assets, boosting demand for U.S. Treasuries and pushing nominal yields down independent of commodity-price channels.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
