  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in crude oil prices raises near-term inflation expectations and term premia, which directly increases nominal Treasury yields as investors demand higher compensation for expected inflation and risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
