  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in oil prices expands fiscal and rent capture incentives for governments, prompting export controls, allocation of export quotas and tighter coordination or direction of producers and logistics to retain rents and manage supply, increasing state direction in the oil sector.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
