  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in kinetic attack intensity elevate volatility and counterparty risk, prompting dealers and nonbank market‑makers to pull back and widen spreads, directly reducing bond market depth and immediacy of execution.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="global_energy_shock::state_directed_economy" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">High-intensity strikes on export terminals, pipelines and refinery networks prompt emergency state takeover, centralized planning and prioritized allocation of remaining oil-sector capacity to preserve exports and domestic supply.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="us_iran_maritime_war::oil_price_level" id="0">
