<edge source="global_energy_shock::contract_enforceability" target="china_us_tech_trade::data_center_build_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Weakened enforceability of energy and infrastructure contracts makes developers unable to secure long‑term, reliable power and service agreements, prompting postponement or cancellation of planned data‑centre construction.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_us_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::contract_enforceability" target="global_bond_turmoil::nonbank_funding_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A deterioration in enforceability of oil‑sector contracts directly reduces the value and fungibility of receivables and collateral used by shadow banks and money‑market funds, prompting higher haircuts and liquidity hoarding that raise non‑bank funding stress.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::contract_enforceability" target="us_iran_maritime_war::sanctions_evasion_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved contract enforceability raises legal and financial risks for intermediaries and shipping firms that facilitate opaque trades, reducing the rate of ship-to-ship transfers, false documentation and other sanctions-evasion activity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
</edge>
