<edge source="global_energy_shock::sovereign_asset_access" target="china_us_tech_trade::capital_investment_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Reduced accessibility of sovereign assets (e.g., freezes, nationalization risk, or limits on pledging state-linked revenue) raises counterparty and collateral risk for financiers, causing banks and institutional investors to pull or withhold funding for cross-border AI infrastructure projects.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_us_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::sovereign_asset_access" target="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved ability to pledge or monetize state‑linked oil assets expands the pool of acceptable collateral for repo and market‑making, lowering transaction costs and increasing bond market liquidity; the reverse (reduced access) tightens liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::sovereign_asset_access" target="russia_ukraine_war::negotiation_momentum" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved ability of external actors to seize or monetize state-linked energy assets produces tangible leverage and funding instruments that can be conditioned on diplomatic concessions, thereby accelerating and intensifying negotiation activity.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_shock::sovereign_asset_access" target="us_iran_maritime_war::maritime_blockade_degree" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater external accessibility/seizability of state-linked assets (i.e., an increase in sovereign_asset_access) increases the targeted state's incentive to threaten or impose formal or informal restrictions on vessel movements and port access to create bargaining leverage and deter seizures.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
</edge>
