<edge source="china_us_tech_trade::regulatory_scrutiny" target="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Intensified cross‑border technology controls and compliance requirements cause dealers and funds to reduce inventories and withdraw from intermediation of securities linked to affected firms, widening bid‑ask spreads and reducing bond market depth.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_us_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_turmoil</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_us_tech_trade::regulatory_scrutiny" target="global_energy_shock::state_directed_economy" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Intensified US/China tech export controls prompt the targeted government to centrally coordinate energy procurement, financing and overseas asset deals through state-owned oil companies to secure supplies and hard currency, increasing the degree of state direction in the oil sector.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_us_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_us_tech_trade::regulatory_scrutiny" target="global_energy_shock::contract_enforceability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">New export licensing, sanctions and extraterritorial compliance obligations create legal uncertainty and risk of penalty for counterparties, causing suspension, repudiation or litigation of cross-border oil contracts and reducing predictable enforceability of those contracts.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_us_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_us_tech_trade::regulatory_scrutiny" target="global_energy_shock::sovereign_asset_access" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened export controls and associated sanctions incentivize onshoring, re‑domiciliation and creation of legal ring‑fences around state-linked oil assets, making them harder for external claimants or foreign creditors to seize or monetize.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_us_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
