<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::policy_rate_expectations" target="global_energy_shock::contract_enforceability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained upward revision in expected policy rates raises refinancing and servicing burdens for oil companies and debtor states, increasing the incidence of moratoria, emergency regulatory changes and renegotiations that weaken predictability and enforceability of commercial oil contracts.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
