<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_liquidity" target="china_us_tech_trade::data_center_build_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A drying of bond market liquidity raises issuance and transaction costs for large project financings, delaying debt closes and construction draws for new data‑centre projects and slowing the build‑out rate.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-12 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">china_us_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_liquidity" target="global_energy_shock::asset_ownership_fragment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A pronounced fall in bond‑market liquidity elevates transaction costs and forces distressed sellers into fire sales, which are typically purchased by a small number of well‑capitalised buyers (often state or strategic investors), reducing dispersion of ownership and increasing concentration.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_liquidity" target="russia_ukraine_war::external_security_coop" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp deterioration in global bond market liquidity forces allied treasuries and defence ministries to prioritise domestic market stabilisation and short‑term financing needs, reducing the pace and scope of coordinated security assistance and intelligence support to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::bond_market_liquidity" target="us_iran_maritime_war::crude_oil_shipments_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher bond‑market liquidity lowers collateral and trade‑finance costs for oil traders and tanker operators, enabling timely financing of voyages and commodity rollovers and thereby increasing the volume flow of crude oil shipments; conversely, liquidity drying up reduces shipments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
</edge>
