<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::nonbank_funding_stress" target="china_us_tech_trade::capital_investment_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Stress in non‑bank credit channels reduces availability of private credit, venture and mezzanine funding—particularly important in China—leading startups and smaller cloud providers to postpone or shrink AI infrastructure investments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">china_us_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::nonbank_funding_stress" target="global_energy_shock::state_directed_economy" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute stress in non‑bank funding channels forces independent E&amp;P firms and private midstream operators to curtail investment or sell assets, prompting governments to deploy state oil companies, emergency directives or targeted recapitalisations to sustain production and service delivery.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::nonbank_funding_stress" target="russia_ukraine_war::wartime_funding_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute stress in non‑bank funding (export credit, private arms finance, commercial paper) dries up private and commercial channels used to finance arms, logistics and reconstruction, directly reducing the volume and timeliness of wartime transfers to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::nonbank_funding_stress" target="us_iran_maritime_war::maritime_security_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising non‑bank funding stress reduces short‑term credit and liquidity available to commodity traders, shipowners and marine insurers, prompting insurers to withdraw capacity and operators to avoid high‑risk transits, which raises assessed and realized maritime security risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_maritime_war</data>
</edge>
