  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Active central‑bank interventions to stabilise bonds/FX (e.g., controls or large FX operations) raise political and supervisory attention on cross‑border flows, prompting authorities on both sides to tighten reviews and restrictions on tech transfers, cloud services and outbound/inbound AI investment.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-12 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">china_us_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_turmoil::central_bank_interventio" target="global_energy_shock::sovereign_asset_access" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded central‑bank interventions (FX operations, balance‑sheet support and capital‑flow management) are frequently accompanied by legal and administrative steps that ring‑fence reserves and restrict cross‑border transfers, making state‑linked assets harder for external claimants to pledge, seize or monetize.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_turmoil</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_shock</data>
</edge>
